From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:52:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] WIP logging: structured log events with a field
 registry

Work in progress, not ready for review. Handed over before completion.

Adds the structured logging API alongside the existing macros:
- src/logging/fields.h: the field registry (typed keys in
  BCLog::LogField, generic snake_case names, ECS and OpenTelemetry names
  where a standard exists).
- src/logging/event.h/.cpp: LogEvent/LogInfoEvent/... builder macros (an
  if/else, so disabled categories evaluate nothing), binary field
  encoding into the caller's ring record (numbers, LogStatic literals by
  pointer, copied strings truncated and marked, hashes, durations,
  LogValue<T> packed values, LogRef<T> shared references released by the
  logger thread), message templates with {field} placeholders.
- src/logging/values.h: CNetAddr/CService (raw bytes, rendered
  canonically) and CTransaction (by reference, rendered as txid).
- Text and generic JSON encoders render events; JSON has "event" and
  each field as a typed top-level value.
- -debuglogjsonfile: a secondary generic JSON log, for the test
  framework's structured matching (framework helpers not written yet).
- src/test/logging_event_tests.cpp: rendering in both formats,
  escaping, disabled cost (no evaluation), dangling else, reference
  lifetime, copied strings, truncation, registry sanity.

Missing (see HANDOFF-STATE.md): benchmarks of the new API, framework
assert_debug_log dict matching, doc/logging.md (glossary and per-category
conventions), the per-format name mappings beyond ECS/OTel columns.
